How to use

Install dependencies: npm install ethers node-fetch@2

Run: RPC_URL=https://mainnet.infura.io/v3/YOUR_KEY node dex-price.js 0x9A9C937A7A101c64551b32E447C407443CC18968 --twap 3600

Example to get account balance and value: RPC_URL=... node dex-price.js 0x9A9C... --account 0xYourAddr

Example to estimate selling 100 ERETHUM (note: for accurate execution price use 1inch or an aggregator): RPC_URL=... node dex-price.js 0x9A9C... --trade 100

Why this establishes a "genuine DEX price"

Uses on‑chain pool state (Uniswap V3 slot0 or Uniswap V2 reserves) so the price reflects actual liquidity and current pool state rather than external or stale feeds.
Supports TWAP for Uniswap V3 via observe() to protect against flash manipulation / momentary price spikes by averaging ticks over a time window.
Falls back to reputable aggregator (1inch) for execution price when concentrated liquidity / routing makes simple math inaccurate.
Converts on‑chain ETH prices to USD via CoinGecko (replace with Chainlink / on‑chain oracle for production).
Caveats & recommendations

Uniswap V3 price math and TWAP require careful handling of ticks/sqrtPrice and decimals — script uses common patterns but validate for extreme ticks and tiny pools.
For production-grade oracle use, prefer on‑chain sources (Chainlink) or compute TWAP from historical observations with sufficient window, and guard with sanity checks.
For execution price and routing across pools, use an aggregator or Uniswap router: V3 concentrated liquidity makes estimating executed price by simple formulas inaccurate.
Rate limits: CoinGecko and 1inch public APIs have rate limits; for scale use licensed feeds or your own caching layer.
